# Path to Redemption on Bot2's Savannah Lions: "Enchanted creature can't attack or block" (CR 508.1c, 509.1b) only for that
# creature. Bot2's Ornithopter is untouched. In turn 3 blocking Bot1's Ornithopter with the enchanted Lions is refused and the
# Ornithopter blocks it (Bot2 takes nothing); in turn 4 attacking with the enchanted Lions is refused and the Ornithopter attacks
# (0 damage, but it is declared: Bot1 is attacked and the Lions stays untapped).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Ornithopter
Path to Redemption
Mox Pearl
Plains
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Savannah Lions
Ornithopter
Plains x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Savannah Lions.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Path to Redemption.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Savannah Lions > Ornithopter)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
! Bot2.Attack(Savannah Lions > Bot1)
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Savannah Lions.Tapped = false
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
